  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Calm conditions are expected to \ncontinue through the next several days as temperatures warm into \nthe upper 80s and low 90s by Thursday. Winds increase Friday ahead\nof an upper level low entering the Pacific Northwest, with gusts \n20 to 30 mph. Winds are expected to be even stronger for Saturday,\nwith gusts of 40 mph currently forecast. Temperatures will also \ndrop starting Saturday as the low center passes through Oregon and\nIdaho. Sunday is expected to be the coldest day of the forecast, \nwith highs in the 60s and low 70s and overnight lows approaching \nfreezing, especially in Elko County. Temperatures are expected to \nrebound to seasonal levels to start next week as the low exits to \nthe northeast.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in warming\ntemperatures through Thursday. Moderate confidence in strong winds\nFriday and Saturday. No changes made to the NBM.",
